Aim: To implement default and static methods in an interface.

Algorithm:
1. Create an interface.
2. Define default and static methods.
3. Implement the interface.
4. Create an object.
5. Call both methods.
6. Display output.
Program:
interface A {
    default void show() {
        System.out.println("Default Method");
    }
    static void display() {
        System.out.println("Static Method");
    }
}
class B implements A {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        B obj = new B();
        obj.show();
        A.display();
    }
}
